{title: Horse and Rider}
{subtitle: Exodus 15:19–21; 15:1–2; 2:1–10; 14:21–29}
{key: F}
{tempo: 120}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [F] | [F] | [F] | [F] |
| [F] | [F] | [Bbmaj7/F] | [F] |
| [Bb/F] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[F]Down by the Nile where the tall reeds grow
A baby cried in a basket boat
[Dm]His sister stood at a [Bb]distance
To [C]see what would happen to him
[F]Then his sister said to Pharaoh's daughter
Shall [Bb]I go and find you a Hebrew woman [Dm]to nurse the child for [Bb]you [C]
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[F]Years of brick and straw and the whip upon the back
Then Moses stretched out his hand and the sea rolled [Dm]back
The Israelites walked through [Bb]the sea on dry ground
[C]And the LORD brought the waters of the sea back over them
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
[F]Then Miriam the prophetess, Aaron's sister
Took a tambourine in her [Dm]hand
And all the women followed her
[Bb]With tambourines [C]and dancing
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[F]Sing to the LORD, for he is highly ex[Bb]alted
[Dm]Horse and rider [Bb]he hurled into the [C]sea
[F]Sing to the LORD, for he is highly ex[Bb]alted
[Dm]Horse and rider [Bb]he hurled into the [C]sea
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
The [F]LORD is my strength and my [Bb]song
[Dm]He has become my sal[Bb]vation
[F]He is my God, [Bb]and I will praise him
[Dm]The God of my father, and [Bb]I will exalt [C]him
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[F]Sing to the LORD, for he is highly ex[Bb]alted
[Dm]Horse and rider [Bb]he hurled into [C]the sea
[F]Sing to the LORD, for he is highly ex[Bb]alted
[Dm]Horse and rider [Bb]he hurled into [C]the sea
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[F]Sing to the LORD
[Bb]Horse and rider he hurled into the [C]sea
{end_of_verse}
